    <div class="keywords-table">
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th style="width: 25%;">Term</th>
                    <th>Definition</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="keyword-term">Composition</span></td>
                    <td>A "has-a" relationship where one object contains another</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="keyword-term">Encapsulation</span></td>
                    <td>Bundling data with methods that operate on it, hiding internals</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="keyword-term">Class Variable</span></td>
                    <td>A variable shared by all instances of a class</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="keyword-term">Accessor Method</span></td>
                    <td>A method that provides controlled access to internal data</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><span class="keyword-term">Protected Attribute</span></td>
                    <td>An attribute prefixed with _ to indicate it's internal</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- OOP SPOTLIGHT -->
<section class="oop-section">
    <div class="oop-section-header">
        <div class="oop-section-icon">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i>
        </div>
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">OOP Spotlight: Encapsulation + Access Modifiers</h2>
    </div>
    
    <div class="concept-explanation" style="background: #f8f9fa; border-left: 4px solid var(--primary-color); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;">
        <p><strong>Python does not enforce access modifiers</strong> like Java or C#, so we use conventions:</p>
        <ul style="margin-top: 0.5rem;">
            <li><strong>Public:</strong> <code>health</code> (no underscore)</li>
            <li><strong>Protected (convention):</strong> <code>_items</code> (single underscore)</li>
            <li><strong>Private-ish:</strong> <code>__items</code> (name mangling)</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">Encapsulation means: access data through methods like <code>add()</code> and <code>list_items()</code>, not by modifying <code>_items</code> directly.</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;"><strong>Composition vs Aggregation:</strong> Inventory is composed inside Player (owned). Aggregation is when an object uses another object without owning its lifetime.</p>
    </div>
</section>

